+# Contract: Rustdoc Ownership & External-Surface Invariance
+
+**Feature**: 001-bench | **Phase**: 1 | **Branch**: `main`
+
+This repository's CLI exposes real external contracts — the `graphhelm` JSON envelope, the MCP tool
+schemas, and the command-line surface. **This feature changes none of them.** It edits rustdoc comment
+lines only, and the one contract it actively restores is the *documentation-ownership* invariant:
+each generated-doc entry must describe exactly the item it sits above.
+
+## 1. Documentation-ownership contract (the contract this feature restores)
+
+The observable contract is about generated documentation (`cargo +1.97.1 doc -p graphhelm-cli --no-deps`)
+and source adjacency. After the fix, for the four affected items:
+
+| Item | Contract (doc attached above the item) | Status after fix |
+|------|----------------------------------------|------------------|
+| `addressable_scope` | Preceded only by "The ONE scope the `execution` verbs can address for a given execution id." block, **including** the `# Errors` paragraph `[`Failure`] when \`execution\` is not a valid identifier.` | Restored |
+| `repository_scope` | Preceded only by "The same addressing rule as [`addressable_scope`] for records that belong to the local repository …"; carries **no** `# Errors` paragraph. | Restored |
+| `assign_schema` | Carries **no** doc comment (pre-merge state). | Restored |
+| `synthesize_schema` | Preceded only by "Closed like every other schema here. `fixture` and `route` are both optional …" block. | Restored |
+
+Invariants:
+
+- **Singular attachment.** A doc line written for item A is never attached to item B. Verified by
+  checking that each `///` run above a `fn` contains only lines about that `fn`.
+- **Signature fit.** Any `# Errors` section appears only above an item whose signature returns a
+  fallible type; any described option/argument exists in that item's body.
+- **Reference validity.** The intra-module link `[`addressable_scope`]` inside `repository_scope`'s
+  block remains valid because both items stay in the same module; the move adds, removes, and
+  rewrites no references.
+
+## 2. External-surface invariance (what must NOT change)
+
+These contracts exist for completeness so a reviewer can confirm the change stays out of them:
+
+| Surface | Defined by | Changed by this feature? |
+|---------|-----------|--------------------------|
+| CLI JSON envelope (the two-face output rule, D-056/#1172) | `apps/cli`, core `protocols` | No — comment lines only. |
+| MCP tool schemas (`assign_schema`, `synthesize_schema`, `wake_wait_schema`, …) | `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs` | No — the `serde_json` bodies are untouched; only the `///` block above `synthesize_schema` moves. |
+| Command-line arguments of `execution`/`mcp` verbs | clap definitions in the command modules | No — signatures and arg structs are byte-identical. |
+| Wire/domain types under `core/*`, checked-in JSON Schemas under `schemas/` | `core/*`, `schemas/` | No — those crates/dirs are not touched. |
+
+## 3. Byte-scoped change contract (SC-002 / FR-006)
+
+A repository-wide `git diff --stat` scoped to the pre-fix tree must show **exactly two** modified
+paths — `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs` and
+`apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs` — and within them only added-and-removed **comment-only** lines
+that are equal as multiset (relocated, not rewritten). Every other path in the repo reports no diff.
