+# Data Model: Restore Displaced Rustdoc Blocks
+
+**Feature**: 001-bench | **Phase**: 1 | **Branch**: `main`
+
+This feature has no persistence and no new domain types. Its "data model" is the **documentation-
+ownership relation** between rustdoc blocks and the CLI functions they describe, plus the pre-fix →
+post-fix state of each affected item. The unit of truth is a source file; the unit of the change is a
+relocated contiguous `///` block. Nothing here is stored — it lives in the two `.rs` files and is
+observed only through source adjacency and generated docs.
+
+## Entities
+
+### Item (an affected CLI function)
+
+| Field | Type | Meaning |
+|-------|------|---------|
+| `name` | identifier | One of the four affected functions. |
+| `file` | path | `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs` or `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`. |
+| `signature` | text | Verbatim `fn` header; determines fallibility and parameters. **Never modified.** |
+| `body` | text | Function body. **Never modified.** It is used to test doc-block content fit. |
+
+Affected items:
+
+| Item | File | Fallible? | Parameters | Owns which block |
+|------|------|-----------|------------|------------------|
+| `addressable_scope` | `execution/mod.rs` | yes (`Result<…, Failure>`) | `&str execution` | "The ONE scope …" incl. `# Errors` |
+| `repository_scope` | `execution/mod.rs` | no | none | "The same addressing rule as [`addressable_scope`] …" |
+| `assign_schema` | `mcp/tools.rs` | no | none | *none* (undocumented, restored to pre-merge state) |
+| `synthesize_schema` | `mcp/tools.rs` | no | none | "Closed like every other schema here …" |
+
+### DocBlock (a relocated rustdoc block)
+
+| Field | Type | Meaning |
+|-------|------|---------|
+| `first_line` | text | First `///` line; used to identify the block unambiguously. |
+| `lines` | list of text | The full contiguous run of `///` lines, preserved **verbatim** (FR-005). |
+| `owner_item` | Item | The single function the block describes. |
+| `fits_body?` | bool | Whether the block's named options/args/errors exist in `owner_item.body`. Must be true (FR-007). |
+| `intra_module_ref` | optional name | e.g. `[`addressable_scope`]` in `repository_scope`'s block; must stay valid after the move (same module). |
+
+### State (per-site pre-fix → post-fix)
+
+The only state transition is *which item a block is attached to*, realized by moving the block's lines
+to sit directly above the owner's `fn`. Signature, body, code line order, and all non-comment bytes
+are invariant across the transition.
+
+## Relationships & constraints
+
+- **One block, one owner.** Each relocated `DocBlock` attaches to exactly one `Item`; after the fix no
+  `Item` carries a line written for another `Item` (FR-004).
+- **Adjacency defines attachment.** A rustdoc block is attached iff its `///` lines are the contiguous
+  run immediately above the owner's `fn`, with no other item in between (FR-001…FR-003).
+- **Code immobility.** No non-comment line changes position relative to any other code line; function
+  order within each file is unchanged (FR-006, spec Assumptions).
+- **Signature/body immutability.** Relocation edits comment lines only; `signature` and `body` are
+  byte-identical before and after (FR-005/FR-006).
+
+## Validation rules (from requirements → observable check)
+
+| Rule | Source | Enforced by |
+|------|--------|-------------|
+| Block sits directly above its owner, uninterrupted | FR-001–003 | per-site adjacency inspection |
+| No item carries another item's doc line; `assign_schema` has no doc; `repository_scope` has no `# Errors` | FR-004 | per-site adjacency inspection |
+| Every doc line preserved verbatim | FR-005 | scoped `git diff` shows only moved comment lines |
+| No non-comment token/ordering/format change; only the two files touched | FR-006 | scoped `git diff --stat` (exactly two files, comment-only hunks) |
+| Doc consistent with signature/body (`# Errors` only above fallible item) | FR-007 | content-fit check (R-2) / generated-docs read |
+| No doubled blank lines / no dropped separator blank | Edge case / SC-003 | scoped `cargo +1.97.1 fmt --check` on the two files |
+| 4/4 items correctly documented | SC-001 | adjacency inspection over all four items |
+| Only relocated lines differ, zero diff elsewhere | SC-002 | repository-wide `git status`/`git diff --stat` |
+| Behavior-neutral | SC-004 | workspace tests unaffected (run only if a wider gate runs) |
+
+## State-transition diagram (post-fix attachment)
+
+```text
+execution/mod.rs                         mcp/tools.rs
+─────────────────────────                ─────────────────────────
+"same addressing rule…"  ──> repository_scope()          (unchanged owner)
+"ONE scope … # Errors"   ──> addressable_scope()   [MOVED from above repository_scope]
+                                                                  "Closed like every other schema…" ──> synthesize_schema() [MOVED from above assign_schema]
+                                                                  (no doc)                              ──> assign_schema()
+```
