+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies - can start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup completion - BLOCKS all user stories
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational phase completion
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Foundational phase completion AND on the Phase 3 relocations existing on disk (T011/T012 observe the post-edit tree); it consumes none of US1's inspection outputs, so once the edits land, T011 and T012 proceed independently of T008–T010
+- **Polish (Phase 5)**: Depends on both user stories being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: No dependencies on other stories; delivers the entire value of the feature
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Independently TESTABLE (its proof — byte-scoped diff vs the T003 anchor plus scoped fmt — is defined without regard to how US1 was inspected), but sequentially ordered after US1's two edits because comparing against the pre-fix state requires the post-fix tree to exist
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Relocation (cut-and-paste of the identified verbatim block) before inspection at the same site
+- Site inspections (T008, T009) may run in parallel once their own site's edit is complete
+- Byte-scoped checks (T011, T012) only after BOTH edits are on disk
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- T001 ∥ T002 (Setup — different observers, no shared state)
+- T003 ∥ T004 ∥ T005 (Foundational — different files/concerns)
+- T006 ∥ T007 (US1 — one task per file, no cross-file dependency; different editors/sessions may take them simultaneously)
+- T008 ∥ T009 once their respective edits land (US1 inspections touch different files)
+- T010 is optional and runs alongside T008/T009 (US1)
+- T011 ∥ T012 (US2 — different observers over the same final tree)
+
